# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/herbalism-alchemy
title Herbalism + Alchemy 1-300
category Professions
kind profession
skills Herbalism, Alchemy
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Herbalism and Alchemy 1-300 together, for both factions: each Alchemy stretch starts with a
# Herbalism step in the areas that give what that stretch needs, which also raises Herbalism, and
# the craft follows with the materials in your bags. Spares carry to the next stretch, and when a
# stretch needs what Herbalism cannot gather yet, Herbalism catches up first. Herbalism ranks are
# trained at the Alchemy trainer visit when the skill allows. Herbalism reaches 300 before the last
# Alchemy stretch.
#
# The Herbalism areas are the Herbalism guide's (the most nodes up at a safe level, listed for your
# level); the Alchemy route, its recipes, trainers, vendor goods and counts the Alchemy guide's
# (enough for 9 players in 10). Anything Herbalism does not give is bought or farmed as there
# (Gather, Buy or Mix).
#
# ASSUMED: how far Herbalism rises on a stretch's materials is the Herbalism guide's expected
# skill-ups per node in the band's areas and what players' recorded gathers gave per node, averaged
# over the band's areas.
# About 24 hours of herbalism in 10 gathering stretches; it gathers about 320 Stranglekelp, 250
# Bruiseweed, 220 Silverleaf, 190 Purple Lotus, 170 Briarthorn and 150 Goldthorn.
#
# Alchemy turns herbs into elixirs, potions and oils. Herbalism is its partner: every reagent below
# is a herb, a vial from an alchemy or trade supplies vendor, or (three times) a fish.
#
# Forever's changes: the healing potions moved to First Aid. Alchemy keeps a Discolored healing line
# that needs a Murloc Eye per potion (a drop) and has no confirmed learn skill, so this route leaves
# it out. New: Minor Arcane Elixir and Elixir of Minor Force (orange to 10), Elixir of Minor
# Fortitude at 50 (trainer), Cerulean Dye and Sulfuric Acid at 40 (Frilled Lichen and Pyrite are
# scarce finds while gathering), Magenta and Viridian Dye, and dozens of new elixirs that are only
# five points wide or sold for Merchant's Favor by Apothecary Durelle near the Crossroads. Several
# Classic recipes kept their spell but changed name: Elixir of Lion's Strength is Elixir of Minor
# Strength, Elixir of Greater Defense is Elixir of Defense, Elixir of Superior Defense is Elixir of
# Greater Defense, Elixir of Detect Undead is Draught of Detect Undead.
#
# Camping: Mana Well (skill 20) is the Alchemy camp item. The Fermenter (skill 140) is a camp
# station from a blueprint that Rath'mael drops in the Ruins of Lordaeron; Shadow Oil, Frost Oil,
# Goblin Rocket Fuel, Ghost Dye and Viridian Dye need it, so this route leaves them out. The
# skill-300 Alchemy Laboratory (flasks) has no known blueprint source yet.
#
# Ranks: trainers teach by tier and train only from their tier's skill: Journeyman at the city
# trainers, from skill 50; Expert only at Ainethil (Darnassus) and Doctor Herbert Halsey
# (Undercity), from 125; Artisan only at Kylanna Windwhisper (Feathermoon Stronghold, Feralas),
# Rogvar (Stonard, Swamp of Sorrows) and, for both factions, Master Mycologist Shurome (the Emerald
# Circle, Felwood: Forever's own trainer, seen training Artisan in players' recordings), from 200.
# Alchemy has no specialisation. Transmutes and the Philosopher's Stone come from Alchemist
# Pestlezugg in Gadgetzan.
#
# The route keeps to trainer recipes from 75 to 265. Holy Protection Potion (100) and Shadow
# Protection Potion (135) would cost about the same, but their recipes come from limited-stock
# sellers (Kzixx, Xandar Goodbeard and Hula'mahi; Harklan Moongrove and Christoph Jeffcoat) and bind
# when picked up, and Holy Protection takes a Swiftthistle per craft, a find on about two Briarthorn
# in five.
#
# Route (crafts are expected counts; yellow and green crafts can take more):
#     1-75  Elixir of Minor Defense, about 82 (known): 1 Silverleaf, 1 Peacebloom and 1 Empty Vial each
#    75-92  Elixir of Minor Fortitude, about 20 (trainer 2s 50c): 2 Earthroot, 1 Peacebloom and 1 Empty Vial each
#    92-135 Elixir of Wisdom, about 47 (trainer): 1 Mageroyal, 2 Briarthorn and 1 Empty Vial each
#   135-150 Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir, about 15 (trainer): 2 Bruiseweed, 2 Briarthorn and 1 Leaded Vial each
#   150-160 Lesser Troll's Blood Elixir, about 12 (trainer): 2 Bruiseweed, 2 Briarthorn and 1 Leaded Vial each
#   160-195 Mana Potion, about 39 (trainer): 1 Stranglekelp, 1 Kingsblood and 1 Leaded Vial each
#   195-225 Elixir of Defense, about 32 (trainer): 1 Wild Steelbloom, 1 Goldthorn and 1 Leaded Vial each
#   225-230 Elixir of Defense, about 8 (trainer): 1 Wild Steelbloom, 1 Goldthorn and 1 Leaded Vial each
#   230-265 Dreamless Sleep Potion, about 43 (trainer): 3 Purple Lotus and 1 Crystal Vial each
#   265-300 Elixir of Greater Defense, about 43 (recipe 1g 30s): 2 Stonescale Oil, 1 Sungrass and 1 Crystal Vial each
#
# Shopping per bracket (vendor goods at vendor prices; gathered or dropped materials by count, enough for 9 players in 10):
# 1-75: Apprentice 10c, vendor goods 3s 28c; gather or buy 87 Silverleaf and 110 Peacebloom.
# 75-150: Journeyman 4s 50c (Classic price), recipes 2s 50c plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor
# goods 8s 68c; gather or buy 50 Mageroyal, 46 Earthroot, 158 Briarthorn and 58 Bruiseweed.
# 150-225: Expert 50s (Classic price), trainer recipes (prices not in the data), vendor goods 33s
# 20c; gather or buy 45 Wild Steelbloom, 42 Kingsblood, 42 Stranglekelp and 45 Goldthorn.
# 225-300: Artisan 4g 50s (Classic price), recipes 1g 30s plus unpriced trainer recipes, vendor
# goods 4g 50s 40c; gather or buy 144 Purple Lotus, 48 Sungrass and 48 Stonescale Eel.
#
# Data: recipes, colours and reagents from the Forever client's tables; trainer learn skills and
# prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists (they reach skill 50-150); vendors, stock and drops
# from data/forever. Materials are valued at about four times their vendor sell price (cloth and
# leather by the square root of it, hides four times higher; tools/lib/professions/materials.js) to
# rank recipes against each other, never as a price forecast.
# Learn skills players' recordings bear out (estimated from Classic's lists; the lowest skill
# players learned each at, never below): Elixir of Wisdom 90 (29 players), Lesser Troll's Blood
# Elixir 125 (18 players), Mana Potion 160 (10 players), Elixir of Defense 195 (9 players),
# Dreamless Sleep Potion 230 (3 players) and Stonescale Oil 250 (3 players).
# ASSUMED: rank level gates Journeyman 10, Expert 20 and Artisan 35 (Classic's; Forever's sniffed
# lists ask level 1 for Apprentice). In-game check: the level each trainer asks.
# ASSUMED: rank prices Journeyman 4s 50c, Expert 50s and Artisan 4g 50s (Classic's trainer lists;
# Forever's sniffed lists price only Apprentice, 10c as in Classic). In-game check: what each rank
# costs.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice (1-75)
section Alchemy 1-75

step Learn Herbalism and Alchemy
  tip Apprentice Alchemy lets you craft up to 75 for 10c, at any character level. Not every Alchemy trainer teaches it: Alliance Alchemist Mallory (Elwynn Forest), Cyndra Kindwhisper (Teldrassil), Ghak Healtouch (Loch Modan), Iaadaria Bitterwind (Zephras Isle), Milla Fairancora (Darnassus), Nyassa Swiftdraught (Zephras Isle), Tel'Athir (Stormwind City), Valiena Swiftgale (Zephras Isle) and Vosur Brakthel (Ironforge); Horde Carolai Anise (Tirisfal Glades), Doctor Martin Felben (Undercity), Kray (Thunder Bluff), Miao'zan (Durotar), Nyassa Swiftdraught (Zephras Isle), Valiena Swiftgale (Zephras Isle) and Whuut (Orgrimmar). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Pair it with Herbalism: Peacebloom and Silverleaf grow in every starting zone, and Empty Vials cost 4c at any alchemy or trade supplies vendor. 1-75 takes about 3s 28c of vendor goods, plus 87 Silverleaf and 110 Peacebloom to gather or buy. Learn Apprentice Herbalism on the same trip: any Herbalism trainer of your faction teaches it at any level, and the arrow picks the nearest.
  train Alchemy Apprentice
  train Herbalism Apprentice
  skill Alchemy 1

step Alchemy 1-75: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 82 Empty Vial (3s 28c); about 3s 28c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Edna Mullby, Eldraeith and Jasper Fel; Orgrimmar: Felika, Kor'geld and Rekkul).
  buy 3371 x82 nearest

step Herbalism 1-15: Peacebloom & Silverleaf
  tip Pick from Herbalism 1 to 15 for Elixir of Minor Defense: this area gives Silverleaf and Peacebloom, and the next one the rest from Herbalism 15. The window lists the areas for your level, best first: the arrow leads to the one you pick and rests once you are in it; each keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns.
